INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal="Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product_line's monthly sales vs its 24-month mean, report top-3 combos with ratio, month, return rate, and assess whether the spike is real demand or channel stuffing. Output a Markdown report saved to disk with source annotations, a data table, and a conclusion paragraph."):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), unique regions, unique product lines, and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute 24-month mean & volume ratio: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_ratio_analysis.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the ratio CSV, find the top-3 (region × product_line × month) combinations with the highest volume ratio. For each, extract the corresponding return rate (退货率) from the original CSV. Save a small summary table to offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate level, (b) whether the spike is a single-month spike or sustained (compare with adjacent months), (c) whether other product lines in the same region also spiked simultaneously. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/anomaly_assessment.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing top-3 anomalies with ratio, month, return rate; (3) every key number annotated with source in format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is real demand or channel stuffing; (5) embed any charts as base64 or reference saved PNGs. All data from local CSV only, no web access → code_agent
